nt resident). Once you submit, you’ll receive an immediate status update and any further actions will be prompted in the Horizon App.\nUser: I've completed this step, continue.\nAI: To proceed, please use the MyInfo service on the secure Horizon Bank web portal. MyInfo will automatically fill in your personal details, saving you time. Ensure your MyInfo account is linked and you grant consent, then continue with the application.\nUser: I've completed this step, continue.\nAI: To move forward, please upload a clear photo or scan of your passport and your most recent payslip using the Horizon App. Open the app, go to the credit‑card application section, tap “Upload documents”, and select the passport and payslip files. Ensure the images are legible; the system will confirm once the upload is successful. After the upload is verified, we can proceed to the next part of your application.\nUser: I've completed this step, continue.\nAI: As a retiree, the next step is to upload your CPF LIFE payout transaction records for the past two months. To do this, log into the My CPF portal, go to **My dashboards → Retirement → Monthly payouts → Monthly payout history**, and download or screenshot the transaction records. Then open the Horizon App, navigate to the credit‑card application section, and use the “Upload documents” feature to submit those CPF LIFE records. Make sure you have identified yourself as a retiree in the application before uploading. Once the upload is successful, we can move on to the following step.\nUser: I've completed all the steps.\nAI: You’ve now completed all required steps for the Horizon Bank credit‑card application. The system will review the documents you uploaded and you will receive an immediate status update (approval, decline or request for additional information) via email or SMS, and you can also view the update in the Horizon App. If approved, the app will guide you through card activation; if further documents are needed, you’ll be prompted to upload them directly in the app.\nUser: Can I track my application status in the Horizon App?\nAI: You are currently in the middle of a request regarding CREDIT_CARDS. Would you like to pause this to look at ACCOUNT_OPENING? I can save your progress and we can resume it later.\nUser: No\n    User Baseline (advisory only; adapt communication only when relevant): Customer is interested in Instant Loan and Horizon savings account. For Instant Loan, eligibility requires age, Singapore residency/citizenship, and annual income; these details have not been provided yet. Next step: provide age, residency status, and income. For Horizon savings account, requires MyInfo verification and confirmation of Singapore residency; phone lacks MyInfo permission and a compliance block remains unresolved, needing manual approval or completion of MyInfo verification in the Horizon app.\n    \n\n    Rules for Text Generation:\n    - Draft a response to guide user to complete ONLY the 'Current Step' with explanation to the current step.\n    - ZERO HALLUCINATION: Rely EXCLUSIVELY on 'Retrieved Knowledge'.\n    - If quoting exact numerical rates or fees, you MUST ONLY use the exact {placeholders} provided in the 'Retrieved Knowledge'. Do NOT invent, alter, or hallucinate placeholders.\n    \n    Rules for UI Payload:\n    - Choose 'uiType' ('chips' or 'none') based on the context to ease user cognitive load.\n    - Choose 'chips' ONLY if the current plan is empty, if 'chips', provide max 2 predicted next actions which can be answered by the retrieved knowledge.\n    - If 'none', provide no UI payload.\n    \n    Output JSON ONLY:\n    {\"response\": \"Your conversational text here\", \"uiType\": \"chips\" | \"none\", \"options\": [\"prediction 1\"], \"advance_step\": true}\n    "}
