 for a Horizon credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Eligibility criteria:\\n  - You are between {{faq_93d37190_001}} and {{faq_93d37190_002}} years old and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_003}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n  - You are older than {{faq_93d37190_004}} years and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_005}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\nOnly Singapore citizens and permanent residents can hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card. To submit an application, go to **More > More for you** within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_f59c2cfe\", \"content\": \"Question: Are payments or transfers counted toward the spend‑bonus interest on my Horizon Bank Savings Account?\\n\\nAnswer: No. Payments and transfers do not qualify for the spend‑bonus interest on a Horizon Bank Savings Account. Only purchases made with a debit or credit Horizon card are eligible to generate the bonus interest.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b70c251f\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to open a Horizon Bank account through the Horizon App while I am abroad?\\n\\nAnswer: - At present, Horizon Bank does not permit account applications from outside Singapore. You must be a Singapore resident and submit the request locally.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"compare, check, review\", \"policy\": \"eligibility criteria, income requirements, age limits, conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"eligibility differences, savings account, credit card\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Eligibility\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c241b12d\", \"content\": \"Question: As a senior citizen, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card, and what are the key requirements I need to fulfill?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we welcome applications from retirees who meet specific criteria. To qualify for our credit card with a credit limit of {{faq_c241b12d_001}}, you must be a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, aged {{faq_c241b12d_002}} or above, have an assessed annual income of less than {{faq_c241b12d_003}}, and not hold any existing credit cards or unsecured loans with us. If you meet these conditions, you may be eligible for our credit card, subject to our standard banking requirements.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c844d766\", \"content\": \"Question: As a retired individual, what documentation do I need to provide to verify my income when applying for a Horizon Bank credit card or requesting a credit limit increase?\\n\\nAnswer: To proceed with your application, please identify yourself as a retiree and, if you are {{faq_c844d766_001}} or older, be prepared to upload your CPF LIFE payout transaction records from the past two months. You can access these records through the my CPF portal by navigating to My dashboards, then Retirement, followed by Monthly payouts, and finally Monthly payout history. Ensure you have the latest version of the Horizon App installed to facilitate a seamless application process.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_fb22bbe0\", \"content\": \"Question: Which transactions are considered eligible spend for Horizon Bank's March